Check that lld-link behaves like link.exe by default: it does not search for a
Visual Studio install from %VCToolsInstallDir% or the like, and a library missing
from the command line and %LIB% is not taken from one. /vcautodetect restores
the upstream search. Explicit /winsysroot and LIB keep working.

# RUN: rm -rf %t.dir && mkdir -p %t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64
# RUN: cp %p/Inputs/std64.lib %t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64

Default: %VCToolsInstallDir% is not consulted, so std64.lib is not found.
# RUN: env -u LIB VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   not lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main \
# RUN:   /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NONE --implicit-check-not="VC toolchain:" \
# RUN:     --implicit-check-not="SDK lib path:" \
# RUN:     --implicit-check-not="UCRT lib path:" %s

NONE: LINK : fatal error LNK1181: input file 'std64.lib' was not found

Default: the VS setup/registry-derived variables are not consulted either.
# RUN: env -u LIB VCINSTALLDIR=%t.dir/sysroot/VC \
# RUN:   not lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main \
# RUN:   /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NONE --implicit-check-not="VC toolchain:" %s

/vcautodetect restores the environment search.
# RUN: env -u LIB VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /vcautodetect /defaultlib:std64 \
# RUN:   /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=FOUND %s

FOUND: VC toolchain: {{.*}}sysroot{{[/\\]}}VC{{[/\\]}}Tools{{[/\\]}}MSVC{{[/\\]}}1.1.1.1

Explicit /winsysroot works with VS variables set and no /vcautodetect.
# RUN: env -u LIB VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/doesnotexist \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsysroot:%t.dir/sysroot \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=FOUND %s

LIB is still searched by default.
# RUN: env -u VCToolsInstallDir -u VCINSTALLDIR \
# RUN:   LIB=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64 \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main \
# RUN:   /out:%t.exe
